# fixedbugs, defect 2428, lane b30-shadow, 2026-11-10 (panel 243's R2, the
# completeness critic's item 16).
#
# A header of the program's own, `both.h`, bound with the first library's
# `pkg-config` group, includes a header of each of two libraries, each named
# like a header the platform holds and each in the folder its own `.pc`
# answers; the second library's group names its header directly. Each header
# is its library's, read with that library's answer; a reading that excused
# only the folders of the includer's own group refused it (route (a), the
# sitting's conservative alternative). It builds and reads both libraries.

extern "both.h" pkgconfig "p2428a"
    constant TIMEB_A: i64
    constant GETOPT_B: i64

extern "getopt.h" pkgconfig "p2428b"
    function b_twice() -> i64

function main()
    print(TIMEB_A)
    print(GETOPT_B)
    print(b_twice())
